# SYNOPSIS

```usage
vx shaders [--check]
```

# DESCRIPTION

`vx shaders` compiles every `.vert`, `.frag` and `.comp` file in the tree, but build output and data, to SPIR-V for Vulkan 1.3 with the host's `glslangValidator`, and writes each beside its source as `<name>.spv`.
The `.spv` files are committed, so a build needs no shader compiler.

A program's shaders also go into a Swift file of byte arrays, an enum with a member a shader (`composeFrag` for `compose.frag.spv`), since programs on the device have no files to read them from:

| Shaders | Swift file | Enum |
| `graphics/loinnir/tests/shaders` | `graphics/loinnir/tests/native/generated/LoinnirShaders.swift` | `LoinnirShaders` |
| `services/radharc/shaders` | `services/radharc/gpu/generated/Shaders.swift` | `RadharcShaders` |

With `--check`, it compiles each shader to a scratch file and fails, naming the file, if a committed `.spv` or Swift file is missing or differs.

# SEE ALSO

vx(1), loinnir(2), radharc(4)

# BUGS

`glslangValidator` must be on the host; without it, every shader fails to compile.
